0LVBNRnd0bEx3NmtwOGF3MVJ5NUZVVkJhQzI3WVh1aVlWSW55WnRfVzhLZnM?oc=5"}, {"title": "Siena Poll Of Likely New York State Voters: Hochul 50%, Blakeman 41% (Hochul 49-39% in August)", "source": "Siena Poll", "published": "2026-09-23T07:00:00+00:00", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMinwFBVV95cUxQWmxURWNXUk8xcVpjY1FFZVMzeWwzZHVDeTJoeVl0NlQ3eThGV0c5bG9ubl9CNmJKWHB4RE5iYlpoM0dJam15amt1MWRIc3BJV0MtdHVhN0RtaEljZ3FxNEFZVEF5NlliWjhGVTEtRVRSby1wSkRzYkFFRnd3RjYtYndXbFFPd0F0YmViTnVWYV9UODc4VTVHbVpRYWFfOVU?oc=5"}], "model": {"prior_margin": 14.1, "prior_sd": 5.34, "poll_margin": 12.72, "poll_sd": 5.41, "poll_weight": 0.49, "fundamentals": {"margin": 14.26, "lean": 6.0, "environment": 4.15, "incumbency": 4.0, "money": 0.11}, "rating_margin": 14.0, "sigma_race": 5.5, "sigma_total": 5.91, "baseline_margin": 13.42, "analyst_adjustment": -1.42, "key_factors": ["Hochul leads consistently by high single to double digits in recent polls in a D+8 state", "Ratings consensus of Solid/Safe D and markets pricing the Democrat near 95%", "Hochul's cash-on-hand and super PAC edge over a well-funded but controversy-hit Blakeman", "Trump stumping for Blakeman and Mamdani stumping for Hochul cut in opposite directions"], "rationale": "September polling from Quinnipiac (+19) and Siena (+9) among likely voters, aggregated estimates in the low-to-mid teens, and a near-unanimous Solid/Safe Democratic rating consensus all point to a comfortable incumbent win, with markets pricing Hochul around 95%. Blakeman's competitive fundraising and a Trump campaign swing are not enough to overcome New York's Democratic lean this late.", "watch": "A tightening in the next round of high-quality polls, or a backlash among suburban moderates to Mamdani campaigning alongside Hochul, could narrow the margin.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["Incumbent Kathy Hochul (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Governor Kathy Hochul enters the final weeks as a clear favorite over Republican Bruce Blakeman. Polls since August consistently show her ahead, with Quinnipiac at 58-39 and Siena at 50-41 among likely voters in September, and aggregated estimates put her lead in the low-to-mid teens. Seven ratings outlets call the race Solid or Safe Democratic, with two at Likely Democratic.\n\nHochul holds the money edge, with about $3.6 million on hand to Blakeman's $3.0 million, and super PACs are amplifying her position. Blakeman has kept the race well funded and landed a Trump campaign appearance, but a matching-funds controversy has drawn negative coverage. Zohran Mamdani campaigning with Hochul is a wildcard for moderate voters. Even so, the state's Democratic lean and the power of incumbency make an upset a low-probability outcome.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9859, "margin": 12.77}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9584, "margin": 9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9776, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9779, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9761, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9756, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9778, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9755, "margin": 11.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9799, "margin": 12.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9796, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9804, "margin": 12.0}]}